From: Prathamesh Shete <pshete@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Jul 2025 04:56:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 127/240] NVIDIA: SAUCE: mmc: sd: Add quirk for SanDisk SR64G
 Extreme Pro power off notify timeout

SanDisk SR64G Extreme Pro cards intermittently timeout during power off
notify operations in suspend, causing error -110 and preventing the
system from entering suspend state successfully.

The error manifests as:
  mmc0: error -110 writing Power Off Notify bit
  mmcblk mmc0:aaaa: PM: dpm_run_callback(): mmc_bus_suspend+0x0/0x98 returns -110
  mmcblk mmc0:aaaa: PM: failed to suspend async: error -110
  PM: Some devices failed to suspend, or early wake event detected

This issue is specific to SR64G cards and occurs when the card takes
longer than the standard 1-second timeout (SD_POWEROFF_NOTIFY_TIMEOUT_MS)
to complete the power off notification during suspend.

Add MMC_QUIRK_BROKEN_SD_POWEROFF_NOTIFY quirk specifically for "SR64G"
cards to skip the power off notify operation and allow suspend to
complete successfully. The card will still be properly powered off
through the normal power management sequence.

This targeted fix ensures only the problematic SR64G cards are affected,
while maintaining normal power off notify behavior for other SanDisk
cards that handle it correctly.

Bug 5318411

Signed-off-by: Prathamesh Shete <pshete@nvidia.com>
Change-Id: I6a55af30a8f1a50f7ef960e5471e16f9499edca3
